IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-sch6-descriptors`
IMPORT `uc4-sch7-descriptors`
IMPORT `uc4-sch8-sch9-treated`

-- Part 5 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), regulations 38 to 40A: whether a claimant has limited
-- capability for work, limited capability for work and work-related activity, or is a severe conditions criteria claimant.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHAT THE TEXT DECIDES, AND WHAT IT LEAVES TO THE SECRETARY OF STATE. Each regulation says a claimant has the status "if it
-- has been determined" that they have it on the basis of an assessment, or if they are treated as having it. The assessment is
-- the Secretary of State's act; this module encodes (a) the status when that determination has been made (a BOOLEAN input),
-- (b) the test that the assessment applies (points, descriptors, causes), and (c) the cases of being treated as having the status
-- (Schedules 8 and 9, in uc4-sch8-sch9-treated.l4). The determinations under Part 4 or Part 5 of the ESA Regulations that
-- regulations 39(1)(a) and 40(1)(a)(ii) also accept are inputs: the ESA Regulations are not among the inputs.

§ `Part 5 — Capability for work or work-related activity`

-- src:743 | PART 5 — CAPABILITY FOR WORK OR WORK-RELATED ACTIVITY

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 38 — Introduction`

-- What Part 5 decides about a claimant, as the record that the other pieces read (`Capability for work`, in the core).
-- src:744 | 38 Introduction
-- src:745 | The question whether a claimant has limited capability for work, or for work and work-related activity, or is a severe conditions criteria claimant, is to be determined for the purposes of the Act and these Regulations in accordance with this Part.
@ref reg 38 (src:744-745)
GIVEN `outcome for limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `outcome for limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `outcome for severe conditions criteria claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Capability for work`
`reg 38 — what Part 5 decides about a claimant` `outcome for limited capability for work` `outcome for limited capability for work and work-related activity` `outcome for severe conditions criteria claimant` MEANS
    `Capability for work` WITH
        `limited capability for work`                            IS `outcome for limited capability for work`
        `limited capability for work and work-related activity`  IS `outcome for limited capability for work and work-related activity`
        `severe conditions criteria claimant`                    IS `outcome for severe conditions criteria claimant`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 39 — Limited capability for work`

-- Paragraph (1): two routes. (a) A determination on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 of the ESA
-- Regulations (inputs); (b) being treated as having limited capability for work, which is paragraph (6) with Schedule 8.
-- The determination "under this Part" is also the input that paragraph (7) reads.
-- out of range: Parts 4 and 5 of the ESA Regulations (not among the inputs): whether the determination was made is a stated input
-- src:746 | 39 Limited capability for work
-- src:747 | (1) A claimant has limited capability for work if—
-- src:748 | (a) it has been determined that the claimant has limited capability for work on the basis of an assessment under this Part or under Part 4 of the ESA Regulations; or
-- src:749 | (b) the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work (see paragraph (6)).
@ref reg 39(1) (src:746-749)
GIVEN `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `determined on the basis of an assessment under Part 4 of the ESA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      circumstances IS A `Sch 8 circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(1) — limited capability for work` `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `determined on the basis of an assessment under Part 4 of the ESA Regulations` circumstances MEANS
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part`
    OR `determined on the basis of an assessment under Part 4 of the ESA Regulations`
    OR `reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` circumstances `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part`

-- Paragraph (2): what an assessment under this Part is about. It concerns a claimant who has some specific disease or bodily
-- or mental disablement; whether the claimant has one is a fact.
-- src:750 | (2) An assessment under this Part is an assessment as to the extent to which a claimant who has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement is capable of performing the activities prescribed in Schedule 6 or is incapable by reason of such disease or bodily or mental disablement of performing those activities.
@ref reg 39(2) (src:750)
GIVEN `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(2) — a claimant can be assessed under this Part` `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` MEANS
    `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement`

-- Paragraph (3): the threshold. "At least 15 points" in three ways: from Part 1 alone, from Part 2 alone, or by a combination
-- of Parts 1 and 2. The first two are special cases of the third; all three are written because the text writes them.
-- src:751 | (3) A claimant has limited capability for work on the basis of an assessment under this Part if, by adding the points listed in column (3) of Schedule 6 against each descriptor listed in column (2) of that Schedule that applies in the claimant's case, the claimant obtains a total score of at least—
-- src:752 | (a) 15 points whether singly or by a combination of descriptors specified in Part 1 of that Schedule;
-- src:753 | (b) 15 points whether singly or by a combination of descriptors specified in Part 2 of that Schedule; or
-- src:754 | (c) 15 points by a combination of descriptors specified in Parts 1 and 2 of that Schedule.
@ref reg 39(3) (src:751-754)
`reg 39(3) — the number of points that gives limited capability for work` MEANS 15

@ref reg 39(3) (src:751-754)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 6 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(3) — limited capability for work on the basis of the points scored` facts MEANS
    (`reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 1 of Schedule 6` facts AT LEAST `reg 39(3) — the number of points that gives limited capability for work`)
    OR (`reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 2 of Schedule 6` facts AT LEAST `reg 39(3) — the number of points that gives limited capability for work`)
    OR ((`reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 1 of Schedule 6` facts PLUS `reg 39(3) — the points scored in Part 2 of Schedule 6` facts) AT LEAST `reg 39(3) — the number of points that gives limited capability for work`)

-- src:755 | (4) In assessing the extent of a claimant's capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 6, it is a condition that the claimant's incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:756 | (a) in respect of any descriptor listed in Part 1 of Schedule 6, from a specific bodily disease or disablement;
-- src:757 | (b) in respect of any descriptor listed in Part 2 of Schedule 6, from a specific mental illness or disablement; or
-- src:758 | (c) in respect of any descriptor or descriptors listed in—
-- src:759 | (i) Part 1 of Schedule 6, as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement, or
-- src:760 | (ii) Part 2 of Schedule 6, as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement.
-- src:761 | (5) Where more than one descriptor specified for an activity applies to a claimant, only the descriptor with the highest score in respect of each activity which applies is to be counted.
-- Paragraphs (2) to (5) together: the assessment finds limited capability for work when the claimant can be assessed and the
-- points reach the threshold. Paragraph (4) (the cause) and paragraph (5) (the highest descriptor per activity) are applied
-- inside the points of `uc4-sch6-descriptors.l4`.
@ref reg 39(2) to (5) (src:750-761)
GIVEN `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `Sch 6 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(2) to (5) — limited capability for work on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement` facts MEANS
    (`reg 39(2) — a claimant can be assessed under this Part` `has some specific disease or bodily or mental disablement`)
    AND (`reg 39(3) — limited capability for work on the basis of the points scored` facts)

-- Paragraphs (6) and (7) are in uc4-sch8-sch9-treated.l4 (`reg 39(6) and (7)`), beside Schedule 8 that they apply.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 40 — Limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- Paragraph (1): the same two routes. (a)(i) A determination on the basis of an assessment under this Part; (a)(ii) a
-- determination of limited capability for work related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of the ESA
-- Regulations (an input); (b) being treated as having the status (paragraph (5) with Schedule 9).
-- out of range: Parts 4 and 5 of the ESA Regulations (not among the inputs): whether the determination was made is a stated input
-- src:764 | 40 Limited capability for work and work-related activity
-- src:765 | (1) A claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity if—
-- src:766 | (a) it has been determined that—
-- src:767 | (i) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part, or
-- src:768 | (ii) the claimant has limited capability for work related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of ESA Regulations; or
-- src:769 | (b) the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity (see paragraph (5)).
@ref reg 40(1) (src:764-769)
GIVEN `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `determined as having limited capability for work related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of the ESA Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      circumstances IS A `Sch 9 circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(1) — limited capability for work and work-related activity` `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` `determined as having limited capability for work related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of the ESA Regulations` circumstances MEANS
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part`
    OR `determined as having limited capability for work related activity on the basis of an assessment under Part 5 of the ESA Regulations`
    OR `reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` circumstances `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part`

-- Paragraph (3): which descriptors the incapability must arise from a bodily disease or disablement for, and which from a mental
-- illness or disablement.
-- src:774 | (3) In assessing the extent of a claimant's capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 7, it is a condition that the claimant's incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:775 | (a) in respect of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b)—
-- src:776 | (i) from a specific bodily disease or disablement; or
-- src:777 | (ii) as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement; or
-- src:778 | (b) in respect of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d)—
-- src:779 | (i) from a specific mental illness or disablement; or
-- src:780 | (ii) as a direct result of treatment provided by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement.
@ref reg 40(3) (src:774-780)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(3)(a) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b)` descriptor MEANS
    CONSIDER descriptor
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 1`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 2`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 3`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 4`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 5`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 6`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 7`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 8`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 15(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 15(b)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 16(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 16(b)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref reg 40(3) (src:774-780)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(3)(b) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d)` descriptor MEANS
    CONSIDER descriptor
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 9`     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 10`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 11`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 12`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 13`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 14`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 15(c)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 15(d)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 16(c)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 descriptor 16(d)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- It is a condition that the incapability arises (a)(i) from a specific bodily disease or disablement or (a)(ii) as a direct
-- result of treatment for a specific physical disease or disablement, for the first group; (b)(i) or (b)(ii) the same for a
-- specific mental illness or disablement, for the second.
@ref reg 40(3) (src:774-780)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
      facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(3) — the incapability arises as paragraph (3) requires for a descriptor` descriptor facts MEANS
    `bodily group and cause`
    OR `mental group and cause`
    WHERE
        `bodily group and cause` MEANS
            (`reg 40(3)(a) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b)` descriptor)
            AND (   (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement`))
                 OR (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific physical disease or disablement`)))
        `mental group and cause` MEANS
            (`reg 40(3)(b) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d)` descriptor)
            AND (   (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement`))
                 OR (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability is a direct result of treatment by a registered medical practitioner for a specific mental illness or disablement`)))

-- Paragraph (4): a descriptor applies if it applies for the majority of the time or, as the case may be, on the majority of the
-- occasions on which the claimant undertakes or attempts to undertake the activity.
-- src:781 | (4) A descriptor applies to a claimant if that descriptor applies to the claimant for the majority of the time or, as the case may be, on the majority of the occasions on which the claimant undertakes or attempts to undertake the activity described by that descriptor.
@ref reg 40(4) (src:781)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
      facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(4) — the descriptor applies` descriptor facts MEANS
    (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors that apply for the majority of the time or on the majority of the occasions`))
    AND (`reg 40(3) — the incapability arises as paragraph (3) requires for a descriptor` descriptor facts)

-- src:770 | (2) A claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part if, by reason of the claimant's physical or mental condition,—
-- src:771 | (a) at least one of the descriptors set out in Schedule 7 applies to the claimant;
-- src:772 | (b) the claimant's capability for work and work-related activity is limited; and
-- src:773 | (c) the limitation is such that it is not reasonable to require that claimant to undertake such activity.
@ref reg 40(2)(a) (src:770-773)
`reg 40(2)(a) — the descriptors of Schedule 7` MEANS
    LIST `Sch 7 descriptor 1`, `Sch 7 descriptor 2`, `Sch 7 descriptor 3`, `Sch 7 descriptor 4`, `Sch 7 descriptor 5`, `Sch 7 descriptor 6`,
         `Sch 7 descriptor 7`, `Sch 7 descriptor 8`, `Sch 7 descriptor 9`, `Sch 7 descriptor 10`, `Sch 7 descriptor 11`, `Sch 7 descriptor 12`,
         `Sch 7 descriptor 13`, `Sch 7 descriptor 14`, `Sch 7 descriptor 15(a)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 15(b)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 15(c)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 15(d)`,
         `Sch 7 descriptor 16(a)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 16(b)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 16(c)`, `Sch 7 descriptor 16(d)`

-- Paragraph (2): limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment: by reason of the claimant's
-- physical or mental condition, (a) at least one descriptor applies, (b) capability for work and work-related activity is
-- limited, and (c) the limitation is such that it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity.
-- Limb (c) is a judgment the text does not assign to anyone by name; it is taken as a fact (an input), never guessed.
@ref reg 40(2) (src:770-773)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
      `capability for work and work-related activity is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(2) — limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part` facts `capability for work and work-related activity is limited` `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity` MEANS
    (any (GIVEN descriptor YIELD `reg 40(4) — the descriptor applies` descriptor facts) `reg 40(2)(a) — the descriptors of Schedule 7`)
    AND `capability for work and work-related activity is limited`
    AND `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 40A — Severe conditions criteria claimant`

-- src:784 | 40A Severe conditions criteria claimant
-- src:785 | (1) A claimant is a “severe conditions criteria claimant” if it has been determined that the claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment under this Part.
@ref reg 40A(1) (src:784-785)
GIVEN `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(1) — severe conditions criteria claimant` `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part` MEANS
    `determined on the basis of an assessment under this Part`

-- Paragraph (5): "NHS services" are the health services continued under the three NHS Acts, and health and social care in
-- Northern Ireland provided for the system promoted under section 2(1) of the 2009 Act.
-- src:797 | (5) In this regulation “NHS services” means—
-- src:798 | (a) health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under—
-- src:799 | (i) section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006;
-- src:800 | (ii) section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006;
-- src:801 | (iii) section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978;
-- src:802 | (b) health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act.
@ref reg 40A(5) (src:797-802)
GIVEN services IS A `Services in the course of which a diagnosis was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(5) — NHS services` services MEANS
    (services's `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service Act 2006`)
    OR (services's `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Wales) Act 2006`)
    OR (services's `health care services provided for the purposes of the health service continued under section 1(1) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978`)
    OR (services's `health and social care within the meaning of the Health and Social Care (Reform) Act (Northern Ireland) 2009 provided for the purposes of the system promoted under section 2(1) of that Act`)

-- Paragraph (3): for a descriptor to be one that constantly applies for the rest of the claimant's life, the incapability must
-- arise from a specific bodily disease or disablement (descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a), 16(b)) or a specific mental
-- illness or disablement (the others) that (i) the claimant will have for the rest of their life, and (ii) has been diagnosed
-- by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of the provision of NHS services.
-- "Health care professional" is the keel's `reg 2 — health care professional` (this is not regulation 98).
-- src:789 | (3) In assessing the extent of a claimant’s capability to perform any activity listed in Schedule 7, it is a condition that the claimant’s incapability to perform the activity arises—
-- src:790 | (a) in respect of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b), from a specific bodily disease or disablement—
-- src:791 | (i) that the claimant will have for the rest of their life, and
-- src:792 | (ii) that has been diagnosed by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of the provision of NHS services, or
-- src:793 | (b) in respect of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d), from a specific mental illness or disablement—
-- src:794 | (i) that the claimant will have for the rest of their life, and
-- src:795 | (ii) that has been diagnosed by an appropriately qualified health care professional in the course of the provision of NHS services.
@ref reg 40A(3) (src:789-795)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(3)(ii) — the diagnosis was made as paragraph (3) requires` facts MEANS
    (`reg 2 — health care professional` (facts's `professional who made the diagnosis`))
    AND (facts's `professional who made the diagnosis is appropriately qualified`)
    AND (`reg 40A(5) — NHS services` (facts's `services in the course of which the diagnosis was made`))

@ref reg 40A(3) (src:789-795)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
      facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(3) — the incapability arises as paragraph (3) requires for a descriptor` descriptor facts MEANS
    (`diagnosis as required`)
    AND (`bodily group and lifelong` OR `mental group and lifelong`)
    WHERE
        `diagnosis as required` MEANS `reg 40A(3)(ii) — the diagnosis was made as paragraph (3) requires` facts
        `bodily group and lifelong` MEANS
            (`reg 40(3)(a) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 1 to 8, 15(a), 15(b), 16(a) and 16(b)` descriptor)
            AND (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life`))
            AND (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific bodily disease or disablement that has been diagnosed`))
        `mental group and lifelong` MEANS
            (`reg 40(3)(b) — the descriptor is one of descriptors 9 to 14, 15(c), 15(d), 16(c) and 16(d)` descriptor)
            AND (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that the claimant will have for the rest of their life`))
            AND (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors whose incapability arises from a specific mental illness or disablement that has been diagnosed`))

-- Paragraph (4) and paragraph (2)(b): a descriptor constantly applies if it applies at all times or on all occasions; (2)(b) asks
-- for one that constantly applies and will do so for the rest of the claimant's life.
-- src:786 | (2) A claimant is a severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment under this Part if—
-- src:787 | (a) the claimant has limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part (see regulation 40(2)), and
-- src:788 | (b) at least one of the descriptors set out in Schedule 7 constantly applies to the claimant and will do so for the rest of the claimant’s life.
-- src:796 | (4) A descriptor constantly applies to a claimant if that descriptor applies to the claimant at all times or, as the case may be, on all occasions on which the claimant undertakes or attempts to undertake the activity described by that descriptor.
@ref reg 40A(2)(b) and (4) (src:786-788) (src:796)
GIVEN descriptor IS A `Sch 7 descriptor`
      facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(2)(b) and (4) — the descriptor constantly applies and will do so for the rest of the claimant's life` descriptor facts MEANS
    (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors that apply at all times or on all the occasions`))
    AND (elem descriptor (facts's `descriptors that will so apply for the rest of the claimant's life`))
    AND (`reg 40A(3) — the incapability arises as paragraph (3) requires for a descriptor` descriptor facts)

-- Paragraph (2): a severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment if (a) limited capability for work and
-- work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part (regulation 40(2)), and (b) at least one descriptor
-- constantly applies and will do so for the rest of the claimant's life.
@ref reg 40A(2) (src:786-788)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 7 claimant facts`
      `capability for work and work-related activity is limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40A(2) — severe conditions criteria claimant on the basis of an assessment under this Part` facts `capability for work and work-related activity is limited` `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity` MEANS
    (`reg 40(2) — limited capability for work and work-related activity on the basis of an assessment under this Part` facts `capability for work and work-related activity is limited` `it is not reasonable to require the claimant to undertake such activity`)
    AND (any (GIVEN descriptor YIELD `reg 40A(2)(b) and (4) — the descriptor constantly applies and will do so for the rest of the claimant's life` descriptor facts) `reg 40(2)(a) — the descriptors of Schedule 7`)
